  "status": "published",
  "title": "Headboard with Reading Lights",
  "summary": "A slatted headboard with two switched LED reading lamps wired inside it.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 6,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Size it for a queen bed: cut two 62 in rails and three 25 in stiles from the 1x4s, and twenty 32 in slats from the 1x3s. Cut a 64 in cap from the 1x6.",
    "Lay out a 62 x 32 in frame with a stile at each end and one in the middle. Glue and pocket-screw the stiles between the rails, checking the diagonals match.",
    "Drill a 3/8 in hole through the top rail 6 in in from each end, and one through the bottom rail at the middle stile. The lamp wire runs along the back of the frame through these.",
    "Lay the slats face down across the frame with a 1/2 in spacer between them. Glue each one and screw it on from the back with two 1 1/4 in screws per rail, then glue and screw the cap on top.",
    "Sand to 220 grit and wipe on three coats of poly. Let it dry before any wiring goes in.",
    "This is a 12 V low-voltage circuit, so nothing is wired to mains. Screw a lamp to the face of each outer slat about 4 in below the cap, push its leads through, and join both lamps in parallel to one run of 18 AWG wire with lever connectors: red to red, black to black.",
    "Run the wire along the back of the frame in cable clips to the bottom rail and connect it to the barrel-jack pigtail. Plug in the 12 V adapter and test both lamp switches before mounting.",
    "Screw one half of the Z-clip to the back of the top rail and the other half level to two wall studs at the matching height. Drop the headboard onto the clip and plug the adapter into the outlet behind the bed."
  ],
